🇺🇸🇺🇦🇷🇺 US Political Theater Ramps Up as "Europe" Plans to take Russia on "Alone"

▪️NATO leadership has talked about a "theory of victory" against a Russian "invasion" and specifically the US not needing to be involved;

▪️Of course Russia is never going to invade - and these plans are instead being made ahead of another Ukraine-style provocation/encroachment on Russia and responding to Russia's attempts to defend itself; 

▪️Be reminded this fits in precisely with US policy including "burden sharing" and "division of labor" between the US and its proxies, especially Europe;

▪️The US regularly performs theater where it pretends to distance itself both from Ukraine and wider Europe SOLEY to manage perception regarding what is in reality Washington's role as the primary belligerent in the war;

▪️ Regardless of episodes where the US has threatened or apparently withheld support to Ukraine/Europe, US involvement in enabling the war has constantly expanded year to year with the only limit being the US' atrophied military industrial base;

▪️Historically, this sort of political theater is performed ahead of crucial escalations the US seeks to contain itself (and only itself) from the fallout of;
